class:: PMMatrixWave
summary:: Arbitrary-size PM network of interpolated wavetable operators
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/FMMatrixUGens, Classes/PMMatrix, Classes/Buffer, Classes/Osc

description::
Replaces the sine operators in the independent FM7-inspired PM matrix with user-supplied cyclic mono tables. The equation is code::y[i] = amps[i] * table[i](phase[i] + sum(M[i][j] * previous[j]))::. Phase and matrix depths are radians. Every internal edge reads the complete output vector from one host sample earlier, including when oversampling.

Tables contain raw cycle samples, not the interleaved wavetable format used by Osc. Lookup wraps around the buffer and linearly interpolates adjacent samples, including across the last/first boundary. Use at least two mono frames. Missing, freed, stereo, fractional-number or out-of-range buffers produce silence for the affected operator; invalid indices never fall back to buffer zero. Global and local buffers are supported. Supernova uses the standard shared buffer lock while reading. Changing a buffer number is immediate and may click; crossfade separate networks for smooth table changes. Feedback and filter histories initially contain zero.

This resembles link::Classes/Osc:: with phase modulation, but uses raw mono tables, double-precision phase, arbitrary-size internal routing and optional filtered oversampling. It is not automatically band-limited: discontinuous tables and strong modulation can alias. Table size, content and oversampling matter.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freqs
Scalar or per-operator signed base frequencies in Hz, including audio-rate values. Size fixes output count N.

argument:: phases
Scalar or per-operator initial radians, sampled at construction.

argument:: amps
Scalar or per-operator amplitude, affecting output and outgoing modulation. Audio-rate supported.

argument:: modMatrix
Exact NxN matrix, destination rows and source columns, in radians per unit source output. Default zero. Control-rate entries ramp over one block; audio-rate entries are read each sample.

argument:: bufnums
Scalar or N buffer numbers/Buffer objects, scalar or control-rate. Each buffer must contain a raw mono cycle; prepare sine tables with code::asWavetable: false::. Buffers may have different lengths.

argument:: resetTrig
Scalar or per-operator nonpositive-to-positive phase-reset trigger. Feedback history is retained.

argument:: resetPhase
Scalar or per-operator radians read on reset edges.

argument:: oversample
Constant 1, 2, 4 or 8. FIR output latency is 0, 15.5, 23.25 or 27.125 host samples. Internal edges retain one host sample of delay.

argument:: smooth
Additional matrix-only one-pole time in seconds at scalar/control rate. Zero disables lag; positive values specify the 63.2 percent response time, including for audio-rate coefficients.

argument:: mul
Output multiplier with standard multichannel behavior.

argument:: add
Output offset with standard multichannel behavior.

returns::
An Array of N raw operator outputs.

examples::
code::
(

    // 2-operator phase modulation using a custom sine wavetable
    Routine {
        b = Buffer.alloc(s, 2048, 1);
        s.sync;
        b.sine1([1, 0.3, 0.1], asWavetable: false);
        s.sync;
        x = {
            var ops = PMMatrixWave.ar([110, 221], 0, [1, 0.6],
                [[0, 1.2], [0.15, 0]], b, oversample: 2);
            Splay.ar(ops) * 0.12 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05)
        }.play;
    }.play;
)
::
code::
(
x.free;
b.free;
)
::


code::
(

    Routine {
        b = Buffer.alloc(s, 1024, 1);
        c = Buffer.alloc(s, 1024, 1);
        s.sync;
        b.sine1(1.0/[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], asWavetable: false);
        c.sine1(1.0/[1, 0, 3, 0, 5, 0], asWavetable: false);
        s.sync;
        x = {
            var modMatrix = [
                [0.5, MouseX.kr(0, 2)],
                [MouseY.kr(0, 2), 0.5]
            ];
            var ops = PMMatrixWave.ar([100, 150], 0, [1, 1], modMatrix, [b.bufnum, c.bufnum], oversample: 2);
            Splay.ar(ops) * 0.15 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.1)
        }.play;
    }.play;
)
::

code::
(

    Routine {
        b = Buffer.alloc(s, 2048, 1);
        s.sync;
        // Sawtooth approximation
        b.sine1(1.0/(1..10), asWavetable: false);
        s.sync;
        x = {
            var modMatrix = [[MouseX.kr(0, 3)]]; // Self-modulation
            var ops = PMMatrixWave.ar([110], 0, [1], modMatrix, [b.bufnum], oversample: 2);
            (ops[0] * 0.15 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.1)) ! 2
        }.play;
    }.play;
)
::
